A||||1||mshill||3.4L installs, don't forget this...||||1||
Z||000000||mshill||01-05-2001||02:31 AM||||This one got me...  I was all set to put my 3.4L onto my cradle (4 speed), and I got it up on the hoist ready to install the clutch when I realize the clutch alignment tool won't fit in the enf of the crankshaft.  OOPS!!!  Forgot to remove the bushing from the crankshaft.  Back on the stand it went and off with the flywheel.  Bushing was out in a few minutes and 30 minutes later I was back where I was before.<P>I told my 12 year old son that was helping me, "Stick with me and you will learn how not to work on cars so you won't have to do everything twice like your old man".<P>It's on now and I can start accessorizing.||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||01-05-2001||02:57 AM||||you only do things TWICE??? My gosh, here at the shop we do things three or four times (always practicing til we get it right!!) -- That's ok, remind you sometime to tell you the story of the fuel pump I installed three times - couldn't for the life figure out why it wouldn't pump fuel (this was on a 3.4 conversion too) -- I could hear it run when I tested it so assumed that all was well.......forgot to take off one of the little white plugs on the outlet of the pump -- didn't notice it when I re-inspected it - darn thing was stuck up inside the hose!! The nerve of that little plug!! -- The point is, it happens to all of us at one time or another!!||||reg||1
